  "goodToKnow": "Der Oberschenkel is the thigh; der Unterschenkel is the lower leg. Der Oberschenkelknochen (femur) is the longest bone in the body, and der Oberschenkelhalsbruch (femoral neck fracture) is a common injury among older people after falls. Der Schenkel also means a chicken leg (Hähnchenschenkel) and a side of an angle in geometry. Sich auf die Schenkel klopfen means to slap one's thighs with laughter. Plural: die Oberschenkel."
